    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T21:45:03Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/2276-aligned-setup-kinds · PR #2279 · pinned by turned_offset2d_cuts_like_the_baked_part, turned_trace_cuts_like_the_baked_part, turned_engrave_cuts_like_the_baked_part, kinds_without_proof_stay_refused_in_a_turned_setup · merges when reviewed\n\nThis is a partial fix (`Refs #2276`). PR #2279 removes the refusal for 2D Offset, Trace and Engrave. The tests turn the part about X and about Z, and compare the path and the posted program with the same part baked turned.\n\nThese kinds keep the refusal. The reason for each kind:\n\n- Slot: `slot_pick::slot_bound_of` reads the picks through `model::transform_of` (the model frame).\n- Trochoidal Slot and Circular: the region comes from `region_for_job`, but no test proves it yet. Their coordinates are typed values, so the proof needs a different shape.\n- 2D Chamfer: the region comes from `region_for_job`. The test needs a picked edge and a chamfer mill in the fixture.\n- Drill, Bore and Thread: the hole list is params data that the panel recognizes from the model. The frame of that recognition is not proved.\n- Deburr: its reads are not checked yet.\n- Probe: `probe_pick` reads the picks through `model::transform_of` (the model frame).\n- The 5-axis and rotary kinds: `selection::drive_chains` reads the model frame. A turned part under a moving tool axis is open design.\n- Lathe, plasma, wire and sinker kinds: the non-mill machine refusal stays.\n\nThe verify check and the post gate do not change. The issue stays open for the kinds in this list.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
